Bootstrap Chain Milestones
==========================

Version  Milestone
-------  ---------
00       Minimal DATA-only bootstrap (129 bytes)
01       First non-standard 6502 mnemonics
02       Source becomes human-readable assembly
03       Byte selectors, label assignments, origin setting
04       Two-pass assembly (forward references)
05       Hash tables for label/instruction lookup
06       Instruction table generator (instgen)
07       Error diagnostics, line numbers, stderr output
08       .include directive, file stack
09       Sections (.zeropage/.code), command-line arguments
10       Local labels, heap-based global label storage
11       Standard 6502 syntax (all 13 addressing modes), forward reference tracking
12       Source transitions to standard syntax (standard syntax migration)
13       Expression evaluation, .data directive
14       .ifdef/.endif conditional assembly
15       Macros, << >> shift operators
16       Data directives, decimal constants, memory protection
17       Self-hosting, .ifndef/.else


Source Syntax Evolution
=======================
Each version's source can only use syntax supported by the version that
builds it. The left column shows new syntax each version can assemble;
the right column shows new syntax first used in that version's source.

Ver New syntax supported             New syntax used in source
--- -------------------------------- ----------------------------
00  DATA $XX, ; comments             -
01  Non-standard mnemonics           None
    (LDA#, STAZ), labels,
    strings, $XXXX hex
02  None                             Non-standard mnemonics,
                                     labels, label references
03  < > byte selectors,              Char escape literals
    label = $XX, * = $XXXX,
    new instrs (BITZ, BMI,
    BPL, SBCZ)
04  Two-pass (fwd refs),             = assignments, < > selectors,
    ~ branches, more instrs          * = origin
05  Hash tables (internal)           None
06  More instrs (via instgen),       None
    flag-based operand types
07  Error diagnostics, stderr,       ZP addressing without <
    line number tracking             (STAZ VAR not STAZ <VAR)
08  .include, file stack,            None
    more instructions
09  .zeropage, .code, ASLZ,         .include
    command-line arguments
10  Local labels (.prefix),          .zeropage, .code
    heap-based global labels
11  Standard 6502 syntax,            None (cannot self-host)
    all 13 addr modes, #'x',
    fwd ref tracking
12  None                             Standard 6502 syntax,
                                     #'x' character literals
13  Expressions (+, -), .data,       .data (replaces DATA)
    char lits as terms
14  .ifdef/.endif, define:           Expressions (+, -),
                                     char literal arithmetic
15  .macro/.endmacro, << >>,         .ifdef/.endif, define:
    optional label colons
16  .byte/.word/.asciiz/.reserve,    Colons, macros, << >>
    decimal, comma-separated
17  .ifndef, .else                   .byte, .word, .asciiz,
                                     decimal constants
